## Basic Record

```java
// Record declaration
public record UserDTO(Long id, String name, String email) {}

// Equivalent to:
// public final class UserDTO {
//     private final Long id;
//     private final String name;
//     private final String email;
//     public UserDTO(Long id, String name, String email) { ... }
//     public Long id() { return id; }   // accessor (not getId()!)
//     public String name() { return name; }
//     public String email() { return email; }
//     equals, hashCode, toString auto-generated
// }

UserDTO user = new UserDTO(1L, "Alice", "alice@example.com");
System.out.println(user.name());   // Alice (not getName())
System.out.println(user);  // UserDTO[id=1, name=Alice, email=alice@example.com]
```

## Compact Constructor for Validation

```java
public record Money(BigDecimal amount, String currency) {
    // Compact constructor — parameters are already assigned, just validate
    public Money {
        Objects.requireNonNull(amount, "amount must not be null");
        Objects.requireNonNull(currency, "currency must not be null");
        if (amount.compareTo(BigDecimal.ZERO) < 0) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Amount cannot be negative: " + amount);
        }
        currency = currency.toUpperCase();  // normalize in compact constructor
    }
}
```

## Records with Interfaces and Custom Methods

```java
public interface Identifiable {
    Long getId();
}

public record ProductDTO(Long id, String name, BigDecimal price) implements Identifiable {
    // Custom method
    public String displayPrice() {
        return String.format("%s %.2f", "USD", price);
    }

    // Implementing interface
    @Override
    public Long getId() { return id; }  // id() accessor satisfies this

    // Can have static factory methods
    public static ProductDTO of(Product product) {
        return new ProductDTO(product.getId(), product.getName(), product.getPrice());
    }
}
```

## Jackson + Spring Boot Integration

```java
// Works with Jackson 2.12+ (Spring Boot 2.5+)
@RestController
public class UserController {
    @PostMapping("/api/users")
    public UserDTO createUser(@RequestBody CreateUserRequest req) {
        // Record used as request body DTO
        User saved = userService.create(req.name(), req.email());
        return new UserDTO(saved.getId(), saved.getName(), saved.getEmail());
    }
}

// Request record
public record CreateUserRequest(String name, String email) {
    // Validation with compact constructor
    public CreateUserRequest {
        if (name == null || name.isBlank()) throw new IllegalArgumentException("Name required");
        if (email == null || !email.contains("@")) throw new IllegalArgumentException("Invalid email");
    }
}
```

## Sealed Interface for Domain Modeling

```java
// Sealed interface — only these three types are possible
public sealed interface PaymentResult
    permits PaymentResult.Success, PaymentResult.Failed, PaymentResult.Pending {

    record Success(String transactionId, BigDecimal amount) implements PaymentResult {}
    record Failed(String reason, ErrorCode code) implements PaymentResult {}
    record Pending(String trackingId, Duration estimatedTime) implements PaymentResult {}
}

// Java 21 pattern matching switch — EXHAUSTIVE
String message = switch (processPayment(order)) {
    case PaymentResult.Success(var txId, var amount) ->
        "Payment confirmed: " + txId + " for " + amount;
    case PaymentResult.Failed(var reason, var code) ->
        "Payment failed: " + reason + " (" + code + ")";
    case PaymentResult.Pending(var trackingId, var eta) ->
        "Payment pending, tracking: " + trackingId;
    // No default needed — compiler knows these are ALL cases
};
```

## Pattern Matching instanceof (Java 16+)

```java
// Old way
if (obj instanceof String) {
    String s = (String) obj;  // redundant cast
    System.out.println(s.toUpperCase());
}

// New way — pattern variable
if (obj instanceof String s) {
    System.out.println(s.toUpperCase());  // s is already bound
}

// Complex patterns
if (obj instanceof User u && u.isActive() && u.getAge() >= 18) {
    sendPromoEmail(u);
}
```

## Event Processing with Sealed Classes

```java
public sealed interface OrderEvent permits
    OrderEvent.Placed, OrderEvent.Confirmed, OrderEvent.Shipped, OrderEvent.Delivered {

    record Placed(Long orderId, Instant placedAt, BigDecimal total) implements OrderEvent {}
    record Confirmed(Long orderId, String confirmationCode) implements OrderEvent {}
    record Shipped(Long orderId, String trackingNumber) implements OrderEvent {}
    record Delivered(Long orderId, Instant deliveredAt) implements OrderEvent {}
}

// Event handler — exhaustive, type-safe
@EventListener
public void handleOrderEvent(OrderEvent event) {
    switch (event) {
        case OrderEvent.Placed(var id, var at, var total) -> {
            notificationService.sendOrderConfirmation(id, total);
            inventoryService.reserve(id);
        }
        case OrderEvent.Confirmed(var id, var code) ->
            notificationService.sendConfirmation(id, code);
        case OrderEvent.Shipped(var id, var tracking) ->
            notificationService.sendShippingUpdate(id, tracking);
        case OrderEvent.Delivered(var id, var at) ->
            analyticsService.recordDelivery(id, at);
    }
}
```

## Text Blocks

```java
// Old way — hard to read
String sql = "SELECT u.id, u.name, COUNT(o.id) AS order_count\n" +
             "FROM users u\n" +
             "LEFT JOIN orders o ON u.id = o.user_id\n" +
             "WHERE u.active = true\n" +
             "GROUP BY u.id, u.name\n" +
             "HAVING COUNT(o.id) > 0";

// Text block — reads like SQL
String sql = """
        SELECT u.id, u.name, COUNT(o.id) AS order_count
        FROM users u
        LEFT JOIN orders o ON u.id = o.user_id
        WHERE u.active = true
        GROUP BY u.id, u.name
        HAVING COUNT(o.id) > 0
        """;  // closing """ at column 8 → strips 8 spaces from all lines

// With Spring Data
@Query(value = """
    SELECT p.*, c.name AS category_name
    FROM products p
    JOIN categories c ON p.category_id = c.id
    WHERE p.price BETWEEN :minPrice AND :maxPrice
      AND (:category IS NULL OR c.slug = :category)
    ORDER BY p.price ASC
    """, nativeQuery = true)
List<Product> findByPriceRange(
    @Param("minPrice") BigDecimal min,
    @Param("maxPrice") BigDecimal max,
    @Param("category") String category);
```

## Modern String Methods

```java
// isBlank() — null-safe empty check (includes whitespace-only)
"  ".isBlank();  // true
"".isBlank();    // true
"a".isBlank();   // false

// strip() — Unicode-aware trim
"  hello  ".strip();          // "hello" (better than trim())
"  hello  ".stripLeading();   // "hello  "
"  hello  ".stripTrailing();  // "  hello"

// repeat() — String.repeat(n) is cleaner than loops
"ab".repeat(3);  // "ababab"
"-".repeat(80);  // 80 dashes

// lines() — stream of lines
long lineCount = multiLineText.lines().count();
List<String> nonEmpty = multiLineText.lines()
    .filter(l -> !l.isBlank())
    .toList();

// formatted() — inline format (Java 15+)
String msg = "Hello %s, you have %d messages".formatted(name, count);
```

